From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt6878: allow unused clocks to gate

The bring-up command line kept every clock enabled, which prevents the
common clock framework from gating unused hardware and causes substantial
idle power consumption.  All currently enabled peripherals now describe
their clock dependencies, so stop forcing clk_ignore_unused.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
@@ -21,7 +21,6 @@
 	// NOTE: Will be replaced by our to-be-bootloader. Keep in for now.
 	chosen {
-		bootargs = "clk_ignore_unused";
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
